HalfTank
========

This project is a derivative work of **CodexMeter** by Raycal
(https://github.com/raycalrui/CodexMeter), released under the MIT License,
copyright (c) 2026 Raycal.

The original project supplied the native macOS menu bar application, the
two-ring quota visualization, the local SQLite quota history with charts and
backup/restore, the Codex App Server integration, the notification pipeline,
and the Sparkle build and release tooling. The visual design and the core idea
are the original author's work.

HalfTank adds:

- OpenCode Go as a second quota source, read through the official `opencode`
  CLI or the console API its credentials already authorize;
- several accounts at once, with Codex logins isolated per `CODEX_HOME`;
- a community reset estimate with a per-signal explanation;
- a pace-aware exhaustion projection reported as a range;
- reset credit guidance that follows a chosen strategy;
- an independent bundle identifier, data directory, update feed, and update
  signing key.

